WEBVTT

00:00:59.002 --> 00:01:01.399
because it had gone
to the neighborhood kids again.

00:01:01.423 --> 00:01:02.575
I was not happy.

00:01:02.599 --> 00:01:03.894
I just wanted to come home,

00:01:03.918 --> 00:01:05.152
eat my fill.

00:01:05.735 --> 00:01:06.921
My mom consoled me,

00:01:06.945 --> 00:01:10.137
and I settled for smaller portions
while she prepared another meal.

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:13.021
Now, I certainly did not
appreciate her that day

00:01:13.045 --> 00:01:15.501
but later realized my mom
was providing a safe space

00:01:15.525 --> 00:01:18.138
and food for people
in the community that needed it.

00:01:18.162 --> 00:01:20.927
(In Yoruba) “Ènìyàn kan lon bímọ,
gbogbo ayé lon tọ́ ọmọ.”

00:01:20.951 --> 00:01:22.861
She was looking after all the children.

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.929
I came to the United States in 1999

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:30.828
and attended the University of Wisconsin
in the city of La Crosse,